# Homecoming — Project Rules

## What this is
A guided self-inquiry web app. Someone comes in with whatever is on their mind — a decision, feeling stuck, low energy, confusion — and the app facilitates a process of dropping beneath the surface-level story to make contact with what's actually true. It does not diagnose, categorize, or prescribe. It holds space for clarity to emerge.

At the end of the process, there is a natural invitation to explore further through coaching.

## Tech stack
- Next.js with App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Anthropic API (for AI conversation, added later)
- Supabase (for database, added later)

## Important: Project structure
- This project uses app/ at the root (not src/app/)
- All pages go in the app/ directory

## Design principles
- Minimal, warm, precise. Not corporate. Not cheesy self-help.
- The tone is honest, grounded, and emotionally intelligent.
- The UI should feel spacious, calm, and intentional.
- No jargon. No frameworks. No productivity language.
- Think high-end meditation app meets clean product design.
- When in doubt, less is more.

## Coding principles
- I am a complete beginner with zero coding experience. Explain what you create and why.
- Build in small steps. Do not do too much at once.
- Use clear, readable code with comments explaining what each section does.
- One component per file.
- Use Tailwind for all styling. No separate CSS files except globals.css.
- When I ask you to fix an error, explain the cause first, then propose the fix.
- Do not refactor or reorganize code unless I specifically ask for it.

## App structure
- Landing page at / (app/page.tsx)
- Entry point selection at /inquiry (app/inquiry/page.tsx)
- AI conversation session at /inquiry/session (app/inquiry/session/page.tsx)
- More pages may be added later

## Naming
- Working title: "Homecoming" (full wordmark: "To Be Alive — Homecoming")
- Name will likely change. Do not hardcode it in ways that are hard to find and replace later.
- The philosophy: most people don't need more advice — they need to hear themselves clearly enough that the right move becomes obvious.
- All copy is placeholder for now. Priority is structure and feel, not final wording.